          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Describe the overall organization and structural progression of the text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 9 · Q14",
          "passageTitle": "Overall Structure — Q14",
          "passage": "Jessica Murray is a researcher who studies\ncanopy soil. Canopy soil is formed in a tree's\nbranches (its canopy) when dead leaves and\nother falling things collect. This material breaks\ndown, becoming canopy soil. Canopy soil helps\npreserve healthy nutrient cycling (how nutrients\nmove through the environment) in rainforests.\nThis benefit is one reason Murray is interested\nin the canopy soils in large bully trees in\nrainforests in Costa Rica.",
